record docwrite.evidence.reader-resize-x11-stress/1 : evidence {
    title "X11 resize stress on the reader: GPU-to-softbuffer fallback rate by fix stage"
    state verified
    result inconclusive
    method manual
    observed_at git:74677babc582e3f94ab342808abacf526e271729
    summary """
        Working tree atop 74677ba, Lubuntu LXQt on X11 (:1), NVIDIA RTX 4060 Laptop Vulkan, debug build, 3-line markdown file, Auto presenter. Stress: xdotool windowsize x160 in a tight loop (80 growing steps then 80 shrinking). With Resized coalesced and presenters resizing lazily, but no lost-surface handling: GPU fell back to softbuffer in 4 of 4 runs ("the presentation surface was lost"). After skip-on-size-mismatch plus retry: 1 of 4 (one retry), 1 of 8 (3 retries), 3 of 12 (8 retries, the committed value). The original code was never run, so there is no true baseline. Window title read "Liminaldoc — smoke.md" via xdotool getwindowname. Visual flicker and lag were not measured or observed; no screenshots or frame timings were taken.
        """
    author "dk"
}

